  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Parliamentary Strengthening Program (PSP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Zimbabwe):  .The Parliamentary Support Program (PSP) strives to strengthen the capacity of the Zimbabwean Parliament to effectively carry out its legislative, representative, and oversight functions more effectively. The activity enhances parliamentary oversight of the Executive and other state institutions and enables Parliament to play a more significant role in improving the lives of its citizens and to exercise more influence in the governance of the country... ..With FY 2021 funds, the activity will:.Strengthen the technical and research capacities of legislators and parliamentary staff in legislative analysis, drafting, policy analysis, reporting, and the implementation of work plans; Support the drafting and submission of two private member bills; Convene meetings between Parliament, government ministries, and civil society organizations to discuss draft bills produced by stakeholders outside Parliament; Provide technical assistance in the revision of Parliament&apos;s Standing Rules and Orders to enhance inclusion and effectiveness in parliamentary processes; Provide assistance to parliamentary caucuses, possibly including the Children&apos;s and Women&apos;s Caucuses, to enhance members&apos; ability to more effectively contribute to the work of Parliament and assume leadership roles within the institution; and Build parliamentarians&apos; capacity to represent their constituencies and the issues and interests of their constituents.. .</narrative>
  </description>
